{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>יכפה</b> — meaning he humbles, like יכפף, as שוגג and משגה, המחוקק and מחוקה; and it is a verb in pausal form (פועל יוצא), standing in place of two, meaning that a bribe brought in the bosom — meaning in secret — humbles fierce wrath. And in this sense he mentioned, that if his cry does not avail him, he gives a gift and a bribe, for they humble anger and wrath, for their nature is to rise up against a man, and a bribe bends them down and makes them submissive."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "Reading ישכילם as 'makes them submissive'; the root שכל here is unusual and the form may be textually uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:00.855321394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}